# XCU batch
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# A batch job runs when the system chooses and mails its completion to the
# user, so the only job a test submits is the command true; it is removed
# again with at -r if it is still waiting. The user may be refused the use of
# batch (the XSI access files); the test then reports UNRESOLVED.

assertion  XCU.batch.001
anchor     utilities/batch.html#STDERR
anchor     utilities/batch.html#EXIT STATUS
class      required
says       batch reading the command true from standard input exits with status
           zero, writes a line "job ID at DATE" to standard error (ID made only
           of letters, digits and periods, DATE in the form of date's
           POSIX-locale format without the zone: weekday, month, day, time,
           year) and nothing to standard output.
test       t/001-submit-message.sh

assertion  XCU.batch.002
anchor     utilities/batch.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/batch.html#OPTIONS
class      untestable
says       batch is equivalent to at -q b -m now: the job goes to queue b, mail
           is sent after it ran, and it runs when the system's algorithm
           chooses.
reason     The moment of the run and the mail depend on scheduling decisions
           that are unspecified, and mail delivery is outside the utility.
